VeridianOS: Xrm: do not use the old buffer pointer after realloc

GCC reported, in src/Xrm.c:

- 1496 (GetDatabase) "pointer 'rhs' may be used after 'realloc'
  [-Wuse-after-free]": when the value buffer grows, the write position was
  rebased with temp_str + (ptr - rhs), reading rhs after Xrealloc() had
  possibly freed it, which is undefined behaviour (it happened to work
  because only the address is used). The offset is now taken before the
  realloc. Real (latent) bug; the result is the same pointer.
- 900 (XrmQPutResource) "logical not is only applied to the left hand side
  of comparison [-Wlogical-not-parentheses]": checked, not a bug. The
  expression "!quarks[2] != table->leaf" is meant as (!quarks[2]) !=
  table->leaf: when bumping to the loose table, its leafness must match
  whether this is the last quark (quarks[2] == NULLQUARK means the next
  level holds values), exactly like the explicit tight-table checks above
  it; the other grouping would compare a quark with a 1-bit flag. Added the
  parentheses the code already meant; no behaviour change.


diff -ru a/src/Xrm.c b/src/Xrm.c
--- a/src/Xrm.c	2026-10-08 17:12:35.353661019 -0400
+++ b/src/Xrm.c	2026-10-08 17:14:22.180096355 -0400
@@ -897,7 +897,7 @@
 		    /* bump to loose table, if any */
 		    table = *(prev = &table->next);
 		    if (!table || table->name != q ||
-			!quarks[2] != table->leaf)
+			(!quarks[2]) != table->leaf)
 			break; /* not found */
 		}
 	    }
@@ -1482,6 +1482,7 @@
 
 	    if (ptr + len > ptr_max) {
 		char * temp_str;
+		size_t ptr_offset = (size_t) (ptr - rhs);
 
 		alloc_chars += BUFSIZ/10;
 		temp_str = Xrealloc(rhs, sizeof(char) * alloc_chars);
@@ -1493,7 +1494,7 @@
 		    return;
 		}
 
-		ptr = temp_str + (ptr - rhs); /* reset pointer. */
+		ptr = temp_str + ptr_offset; /* reset pointer. */
 		rhs = temp_str;
 		ptr_max = rhs + alloc_chars - 4;
 	    }
